text:
Redmine issue #44623. When a wiki page includes another page with the `{{include(Page)}}` macro, the headings of the included page get "Edit this section" links, as if they were sections of the current page. The section numbers of the page then shift: the edit link of a local heading after the include points to the wrong section number, so the user edits the wrong part of the page.

Fix it: headings that come from the output of a macro like `include` must not get section edit links and must not count as sections of the page. Headings in the output of the `collapse` macro are part of the page text, so they must keep their edit links. Let a macro declare this when it is defined, with a `:sections => true` option (only `collapse` uses it today); macros without it are treated like `include`. The included headings are still rendered normally.

Done when:
- on a page with local headings and an included page, only the local headings get edit links, and their section numbers match the numbers used when editing the page;
- the change is covered by tests;
- the existing test suite still passes.
